    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0670" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg664"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            von Holleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state for your
                    information that I am in receipt of a telegram of the 6th instant from the U. S.
                    vice consul-general at Apia, which reads as follows:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Chief justice notified by consuls. Refuses compliance with directions of
                        three powers respecting survey and register fees.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
